ἔσχατος, -η, -ον 
[in LXX chiefly for אַחֲרִית אַחֲרוֹן ;] 
last, utmost, extreme; 
__(a) of place: of the lowest or least honoured place, Luk.14.9-10; τ. ἔσχατον, with genitive part., Act.1.8; 13.47; 
__(b) of time: Mat.20.12, 14, Mrk.12.6, 22, opposite to πρῶτος, Mat.20.8, 1Co.15.45, Rev.2.19, al.; τὰ ἔ. καὶ T. πρῶτα, Mat.12.45, Luk.11.26, 2Pe.2.20; of the Eternal, ὁ πρῶτος καὶ ὁ ἔ., Rev.1.17; 2.8; 22.13; in…
